       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4,250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg/day, which is about five times the usual maximum for metformin. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, and the maximum single dose is typically 850 to 1,000 mg. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possibilities:\n- **425 mg**, which isn't a standard strength.\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg**, with a different frequency.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose, ideally with your resident or attending. For a new start, the usual approach is 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, titrated up as tolerated. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
